-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore): the seat of the person who owns a television (or a radio, or a satellite dish).
--
-- FORWARD-LOOKING ROW, TARGET unstable.  Not the answer of record, and not deployable on Legalese Cloud until
-- `main` has the time built-ins.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom the law is applied -- someone who has a television, radio or satellite dish at
-- home and asks what the Act required of them.  Each question takes the KIND of receiver as a plain input, so the
-- answer shows for each: television, radio (the First Schedule's "broadcast sound receiver"; AM and FM are not
-- told apart by the Act) and satellite dish (its "TVRO system").
--
-- EVERY question takes TWO DATES as plain inputs and pins both axes with the built-ins inside:
--   the day you are asking about  -> EVAL UNDER VALID TIME   (the conduct day; RULES EFFECTIVE DATE follows it)
--   the day the law is to be read -> EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME  (the reading day; TODAY reads it)
-- The reading day matters because S 549/2012, published on 31 October 2012, took the television and radio
-- receivers out of the First Schedule retrospectively from 1 January 2011: the answer for the same conduct
-- differs between a reader on 1 August 2012 and a reader on 1 November 2012.
--
-- A reading day BEFORE the conduct day is allowed and answers "the law as it read on that day, applied to a day
-- still to come".  It does not promise the law will not change before then.
--
-- The facts are ones the person can state.  The Act's own figures (the $40,000 fine, the 3 years) are the
-- Act's; the seat does not ask for them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgbau-nouns`
IMPORT `sgbau-first-schedule`
IMPORT `sgbau-act`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

§ `Helpers: what the person states, as the Act's own records`

-- Not exported.  Each builds a record from plain facts; no field is left to a placeholder.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of receiver`
GIVETH AN Apparatus
`the apparatus of the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN television THEN Apparatus WITH
        `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`  IS TRUE
        `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`                             IS FALSE
        `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`                  IS TRUE
        `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`            IS FALSE
    WHEN radio THEN Apparatus WITH
        `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`  IS TRUE
        `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`                             IS TRUE
        `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`                  IS FALSE
        `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`            IS FALSE
    WHEN `satellite dish` THEN Apparatus WITH
        `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`  IS TRUE
        `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`                             IS FALSE
        `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`                  IS FALSE
        `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`            IS TRUE

GIVEN pictures IS A BOOLEAN
      sound IS A BOOLEAN
      `anyone with equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Transmission
`the transmission described by` MEANS Transmission WITH
    `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`    IS pictures
    `comprises a sound programme for reception`                                                       IS sound
    `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`  IS pictures AND sound
    `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`                                    IS `anyone with equipment`

GIVEN installed IS A BOOLEAN
      `sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `operated` IS A BOOLEAN
      received IS A Transmission
      licensed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Conduct
`the conduct described by` MEANS Conduct WITH
    `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore`   IS installed
    `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale`     IS `sold`
    `operates it, or has it on premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person`           IS `operated`
    `what is received on or by it`                                                              IS received
    `acts under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`                      IS licensed

§ `1. Did I need a licence?`

@export Did I need a broadcasting apparatus licence for my television, radio or satellite dish on a given day, as the law is read on a given day?
GIVEN `the day you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you had the apparatus, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD), for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day the law is to be read` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which the law is to be read, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD): today, or an earlier day such as the day you were told the position.
      `the kind of receiver you have` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc The kind of receiver you are asking about: one of television, radio, satellite dish.
      `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include pictures.
      `broadcasts with sound are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include sound.
      `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes are sent out for reception by anyone who has suitable equipment, rather than privately to one person.
      `you installed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you installed the apparatus in a place, or on a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore.
      `you imported or sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you imported the apparatus, offered it for sale, sold it, or kept it with a view to sale.
      `you operate it or have it on your premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you operate the apparatus, or have it on premises in Singapore that you own or occupy.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Did I need a licence for my apparatus` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` `the day the law is to be read`
        (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` `the day you are asking about`
            (`s 20(1) requires a licence`
                (`the apparatus of the kind` `the kind of receiver you have`)
                (`the conduct described by` `you installed it` `you imported or sold it` `you operate it or have it on your premises`
                    (`the transmission described by` `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` `broadcasts with sound are received on it` `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment`)
                    FALSE)))   -- placeholder: this question does not read the licence field (s 20(1) requires a licence, whoever holds one)

§ `2. If I had no licence, could I have been prosecuted?`
-- This group only arises for someone who did not hold a licence on the day.  The form can ask "Did you hold a
-- licence under section 20 on that day?" before showing it.

@export Would having my television, radio or satellite dish without a licence on a given day have been an offence under section 47, as the law is read on a given day?
GIVEN `the day you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you had the apparatus, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD), for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day the law is to be read` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which the law is to be read, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD): today, or an earlier day such as the day you were told the position.
      `the kind of receiver you have` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc The kind of receiver you are asking about: one of television, radio, satellite dish.
      `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include pictures.
      `broadcasts with sound are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include sound.
      `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes are sent out for reception by anyone who has suitable equipment, rather than privately to one person.
      `you installed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you installed the apparatus in a place, or on a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore.
      `you imported or sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you imported the apparatus, offered it for sale, sold it, or kept it with a view to sale.
      `you operate it or have it on your premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you operate the apparatus, or have it on premises in Singapore that you own or occupy.
      `you held a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a licence granted under section 20 of the Broadcasting Act and acted in accordance with it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Would the apparatus without a licence have been an offence` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` `the day the law is to be read`
        (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` `the day you are asking about`
            (`s 47 offence is committed`
                (`the apparatus of the kind` `the kind of receiver you have`)
                (`the conduct described by` `you installed it` `you imported or sold it` `you operate it or have it on your premises`
                    (`the transmission described by` `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` `broadcasts with sound are received on it` `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment`)
                    `you held a licence`)))

@export What is the most I could have been fined under section 47 for my television, radio or satellite dish on a given day, as the law is read on a given day?
GIVEN `the day you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you had the apparatus, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD), for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day the law is to be read` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which the law is to be read, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD): today, or an earlier day such as the day you were told the position.
      `the kind of receiver you have` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc The kind of receiver you are asking about: one of television, radio, satellite dish.
      `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include pictures.
      `broadcasts with sound are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include sound.
      `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes are sent out for reception by anyone who has suitable equipment, rather than privately to one person.
      `you installed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you installed the apparatus in a place, or on a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore.
      `you imported or sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you imported the apparatus, offered it for sale, sold it, or kept it with a view to sale.
      `you operate it or have it on your premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you operate the apparatus, or have it on premises in Singapore that you own or occupy.
      `you held a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a licence granted under section 20 of the Broadcasting Act and acted in accordance with it.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I could have been fined` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` `the day the law is to be read`
        (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` `the day you are asking about`
            (`s 47 greatest fine in dollars`
                (`the apparatus of the kind` `the kind of receiver you have`)
                (`the conduct described by` `you installed it` `you imported or sold it` `you operate it or have it on your premises`
                    (`the transmission described by` `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` `broadcasts with sound are received on it` `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment`)
                    `you held a licence`)))

§ `3. Which text of the First Schedule applied to me?`

@export Which text of the First Schedule of the Broadcasting Act governed conduct on a given day, as the law is read on a given day?
GIVEN `the day you are asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you had the apparatus, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD), for example 2011-06-01.
      `the day the law is to be read` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which the law is to be read, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD): today, or an earlier day such as the day you were told the position.
GIVETH A `Version of the First Schedule`
`Which text of the First Schedule applied` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` `the day the law is to be read`
        (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` `the day you are asking about`
            `the version of the First Schedule that governs`)

§ `4. Over a period`
-- This group only arises for someone who had the apparatus for more than one day, or who is unsure of the day.

@export Was there any day in a period on which I needed a broadcasting apparatus licence for my television, radio or satellite dish, as the law is read on a given day?
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the period you are asking about, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD).
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period you are asking about, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD).
      `the day the law is to be read` IS A DATE @desc The day as at which the law is to be read, as a date (YYYY-MM-DD): today, or an earlier day such as the day you were told the position.
      `the kind of receiver you have` IS A `Kind of receiver` @desc The kind of receiver you are asking about: one of television, radio, satellite dish.
      `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include pictures.
      `broadcasts with sound are received on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes received on or by the apparatus include sound.
      `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the programmes are sent out for reception by anyone who has suitable equipment, rather than privately to one person.
      `you installed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you installed the apparatus in a place, or on a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore.
      `you imported or sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you imported the apparatus, offered it for sale, sold it, or kept it with a view to sale.
      `you operate it or have it on your premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you operate the apparatus, or have it on premises in Singapore that you own or occupy.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Did I need a licence on any day in the period` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` `the day the law is to be read`
        (`EVER BETWEEN` `the first day of the period` `the last day of the period`
            (GIVEN day YIELD
                `s 20(1) requires a licence`
                    (`the apparatus of the kind` `the kind of receiver you have`)
                    (`the conduct described by` `you installed it` `you imported or sold it` `you operate it or have it on your premises`
                        (`the transmission described by` `broadcasts with pictures are received on it` `broadcasts with sound are received on it` `the programmes are for anyone with the equipment`)
                        FALSE)))   -- placeholder: this question does not read the licence field
